<article class="env-lemma" id="09GV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09GV">Lemma <span data-tag="09GV">9.10.6</span>.</a> Any two algebraic closures of a field are isomorphic. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $F$ be a field. If $M$ and $\overline{F}$ are algebraic closures of $F$, then there exists a morphism of $F$-extensions $\varphi : M \to \overline{F}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/09GU" data-tag="09GU">9.10.5</a>. Now the image $\varphi (M)$ is algebraically closed. On the other hand, the extension $\varphi (M) \subset \overline{F}$ is algebraic by Lemma <a href="/tag/09GF" data-tag="09GF">9.8.4</a>. Thus $\varphi (M) = \overline{F}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>